{"schemaVersion":1,"generatedAt":"2026-08-16T16:20:46.501Z","id":"0d7b38c19237e5ab6cd8c3ef","canonicalUrl":"https://lore.kernel.org/r/tencent_E5954D5C14D99713A73E3121B97EEDA6170A%40qq.com/","channels":["lkml"],"thread":{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"thread:lore-git:tencent_E5954D5C14D99713A73E3121B97EEDA6170A@qq.com","source":{"kind":"static-generated","canonicalThreadUrl":"https://lore.kernel.org/r/tencent_E5954D5C14D99713A73E3121B97EEDA6170A%40qq.com/","fetchedAt":"2026-08-16T16:20:46.501Z","contentDigest":"lore-git:tencent_E5954D5C14D99713A73E3121B97EEDA6170A@qq.com"},"subject":"Re: [PATCH v2] Bluetooth: ISO: fix use-after-free of listener socket in iso_conn_ready","messages":{"cd71d83c71abbd0cdba00c0aa9160d421e7c28d4.camel@iki.fi":{"id":"cd71d83c71abbd0cdba00c0aa9160d421e7c28d4.camel@iki.fi","messageId":"cd71d83c71abbd0cdba00c0aa9160d421e7c28d4.camel@iki.fi","references":["tencent_E5954D5C14D99713A73E3121B97EEDA6170A@qq.com"],"missingAncestorIds":["tencent_E5954D5C14D99713A73E3121B97EEDA6170A@qq.com"],"author":{"name":"Pauli Virtanen","address":"pav@iki.fi"},"replyTo":[],"to":[{"name":"Hang Nan","address":"2122295973@qq.com"},{"name":"","address":"linux-bluetooth@vger.kernel.org"}],"cc":[{"name":"Marcel Holtmann","address":"marcel@holtmann.org"},{"name":"Luiz Augusto von Dentz","address":"luiz.dentz@gmail.com"},{"name":"","address":"linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"stable@vger.kernel.org"}],"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-16T14:26:03.000Z","iso":"2026-08-16T14:26:03.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"Re: [PATCH v2] Bluetooth: ISO: fix use-after-free of listener socket in iso_conn_ready","mailingLists":[{"id":"linux-kernel.vger.kernel.org","displayName":"linux-kernel.vger.kernel.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"to, 2026-08-13 kello 19:39 +0800, Hang Nan kirjoitti:"},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"iso_conn_ready() looks up the BIS listener socket with iso_get_sock(),"},{"depth":1,"text":"which takes a reference, and then, without re-checking its state,"},{"depth":1,"text":"creates a child socket from it:"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"    parent = iso_get_sock(hdev, ...);"},{"depth":1,"text":"    if (!parent)"},{"depth":1,"text":"        return;"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"    lock_sock(parent);"},{"depth":1,"text":"    sk = iso_sock_alloc(sock_net(parent), NULL, BTPROTO_ISO, ...);"},{"depth":1,"text":"    ..."},{"depth":1,"text":"    iso_chan_add(conn, sk, parent);"},{"depth":1,"text":"    ..."},{"depth":1,"text":"    release_sock(parent);"},{"depth":1,"text":"    sock_put(parent);"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"If the listener socket is closed concurrently, between iso_get_sock()"},{"depth":1,"text":"and lock_sock(), the reference taken by iso_get_sock() may be the last"},{"depth":1,"text":"one: the close path drops the link-list reference, and once"},{"depth":1,"text":"iso_conn_ready() drops its own reference at the end of the function the"},{"depth":1,"text":"socket is freed.  The child socket, however, is already linked to the"},{"depth":1,"text":"freed parent, and a later disconnect of the child runs iso_chan_del()"},{"depth":1,"text":"-> bt_accept_unlink(), which dereferences the dangling parent pointer"},{"depth":1,"text":"into the freed accept queue (a use-after-free).  The same dangling"},{"depth":1,"text":"pointer is also dereferenced through parent->***() in"},{"depth":1,"text":"iso_chan_del()."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Fix it the same way the connected (non-BIS) path was fixed in commit"},{"depth":1,"text":"0d255e63fcf3 (\"Bluetooth: ISO: hold sk properly in iso_conn_ready\"):"},{"depth":1,"text":"after taking the socket lock, re-check that the parent is still a"},{"depth":1,"text":"listening, alive socket, and bail out otherwise."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Fixes: ccf74f2390d60 (\"Bluetooth: Add BTPROTO_ISO socket type\")"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Changes in v2:"},{"depth":1,"text":"- Fix GitLint B3: replace hard tabs with spaces in the commit message"},{"depth":1,"text":"  code snippet (no functional change)"}],"lineCount":38,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Changelog should not be in the commit message, but below the --- line."},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"Signed-off-by: Hang Nan <2122295973@qq.com>"},{"depth":1,"text":"---"},{"depth":1,"text":" net/bluetooth/iso.c | 15 +++++++++++++++"},{"depth":1,"text":" 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"diff --git a/net/bluetooth/iso.c b/net/bluetooth/iso.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"index aa2ce78f56a2..069fc87a4e18 100644"},{"depth":1,"text":"--- a/net/bluetooth/iso.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"+++ b/net/bluetooth/iso.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -2277,6 +2277,21 @@ static void iso_conn_ready(struct iso_conn *conn)"},{"depth":1,"text":" "},{"depth":1,"text":" \t\tlock_sock(parent);"},{"depth":1,"text":" "},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t/* The listener socket may have been closed concurrently"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t * between iso_get_sock() and lock_sock(): the reference"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t * taken by iso_get_sock() may be the last one, in which"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t * case the socket is freed as soon as we drop it at the"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t * end of this function.  Recheck that the parent is still"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t * a valid, listening socket before creating a child"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t * socket from it."},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t */"}],"lineCount":21,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"The explanations are long. Assisted-by: some LLM?"},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\tif (parent->sk_state != BT_LISTEN ||"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t    sock_flag(parent, SOCK_ZAPPED)) {"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\trelease_sock(parent);"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\tsock_put(parent);"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\treturn;"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t}"}],"lineCount":6,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"The change itsef looks good to me."},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"+"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t\tsk = iso_sock_alloc(sock_net(parent), NULL,"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t\t\t\t    BTPROTO_ISO, GFP_ATOMIC, 0);"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t\tif (!sk) {"}],"lineCount":4,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"signature","text":"Pauli Virtanen","lineCount":1}],"patchIds":[],"attachmentMetadata":[],"sourceOrdinal":0,"diagnostics":[],"declaredParentMessageId":"tencent_E5954D5C14D99713A73E3121B97EEDA6170A@qq.com"}},"rootIds":["cd71d83c71abbd0cdba00c0aa9160d421e7c28d4.camel@iki.fi"],"childrenByParent":{},"chronologicalIds":["cd71d83c71abbd0cdba00c0aa9160d421e7c28d4.camel@iki.fi"],"patchSeries":[],"diagnostics":[],"patches":{}}}